Theorem DP-7: is_rc_skip_eligible truth table — pure-state portion (callee parameter scope)

  Preconditions:
    - s is a canonical AimsState per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
    - is_rc_skip_eligible : AimsState -> Bool per Annex E §AIMS DP-7 +
      Appendix C truth table
    - DP-7 is a pure boolean predicate over (Locality x Access x Consumption
      x Cardinality x Uniqueness x is_scalar); Shape / Effect are
      non-load-bearing
    - Scope clarification: DP-7 evaluated on CALLEE's parameter state. The
      callee parameter may be FunctionLocal even when caller's arg is
      ArgEscaping because parameter contract reflects callee USE (per
      Annex E §AIMS TF-11 Apply row + Annex E §AIMS DP-7 scope clause).
      ArgEscaping floor in TF-11 applies to CALLER's arg, not callee's
      contract.
    - Uniqueness = Unique clause is load-bearing — Shared+Linear+Once is the
      negative-direction witness (caller inc never balanced -> leak).
    - is_local(s) per DP-8: locality in {BlockLocal, FunctionLocal}.
      Required as DP-7 conjunct via Annex E §AIMS DP-7 +
      Appendix C row 1 condition.
    - CN-1 canonical invariant: Consumption = Dead iff Cardinality = Absent.
    - CN-6 canonical invariant: Locality >= HeapEscaping AND Uniqueness =
      Unique -> Uniqueness := MaybeShared (wide-locality uniqueness ceiling).
    - CN-8 canonical invariant: Access = Borrowed AND Locality > FunctionLocal
      -> Locality := FunctionLocal.

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState (canonical).
      is_rc_skip_eligible(s)
        <=> (is_local(s)
              AND s.access = Owned
              AND s.consumption = Linear
              AND s.cardinality = Once
              AND s.uniqueness = Unique
              AND NOT is_scalar(s))

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Exhaustive enumeration over the 6-tuple product per Appendix C
          truth table: 5 Locality x 2 Access x 4 Consumption x 3 Cardinality
          x 3 Uniqueness x 2 is_scalar = 720 candidate input states.
      (b) Soundness equality on every canonical row + reachable-subset
          enumeration via CN-1 + CN-6 + CN-8 canonicalization filters.

    Part (a) — Appendix C row partition (7 rows, exhaustive):
      Row 1: is_local(s) = false (Locality in {ArgEscaping, HeapEscaping,
        Unknown}) -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (first conjunct fails). ArgEscaping
        explicitly excluded per DP-8 — see DP-8 proof + Annex E §AIMS
        DP-8 rationale (ArgEscaping optimization is stack promotion in
        caller via RL-15a, NOT RC elision).
      Row 2: is_local = true, Access = Borrowed -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (second conjunct fails). Borrowed values
        never own their RC; caller inc + callee dec asymmetric.
      Row 3: is_local = true, Owned, Consumption != Linear -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (third conjunct fails). Affine /
        Unrestricted / Dead cannot guarantee inc/dec pair cancellation.
      Row 4: is_local = true, Owned, Linear, Cardinality != Once -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (fourth conjunct fails). Many uses or
        Absent (Dead) break the move-once contract.
      Row 5: is_local = true, Owned, Linear, Once, Uniqueness != Unique -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (fifth conjunct fails). Negative-direction
        witness: Shared+Linear+Once caller arg unbalances inc/dec (caller's
        inc fires; callee skips dec; aliased value's refcount drifts to
        leak).
      Row 6: is_local = true, Owned, Linear, Once, Unique, is_scalar = true -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (sixth conjunct fails). SCALAR carries
        no RC ops by L-9; skip-eligibility tautologically irrelevant.
      Row 7: is_local = true, Owned, Linear, Once, Unique, is_scalar = false -> true
        Soundness: predicate true (all six conjuncts hold). Caller emits
        RcInc on Owned param; callee's RcDec at parameter death exactly
        cancels; per Annex E §AIMS RL-3 the pair is elided when DP-7
        eligibility holds.

    Part (b) — canonical subset filter + coverage gate:
      Pre-canonical enumeration: 5 x 2 x 4 x 3 x 3 x 2 = 720 product states.
      Canonical filters applied in §2 ordering (CN-8 -> CN-6 -> CN-1):
        CN-1 (Consumption = Dead iff Cardinality = Absent):
          Excludes Dead AND non-Absent + non-Dead AND Absent. Of 4 Consumption
          x 3 Cardinality = 12 combinations, canonical = 7 (Dead+Absent +
          3 non-Dead Consumption x Once + 3 non-Dead Consumption x Many).
        CN-6 (Locality >= HeapEscaping AND Uniqueness = Unique):
          Excludes Locality in {HeapEscaping, Unknown} AND Uniqueness =
          Unique combinations. (CN-6 demotes Unique -> MaybeShared, so
          these states canonicalize away from Unique.)
        CN-8 (Borrowed AND Locality > FunctionLocal):
          Clamps Borrowed + (ArgEscaping | HeapEscaping | Unknown) ->
          Borrowed + FunctionLocal. Excludes Borrowed in 3 wide-locality
          combinations.
      Canonical reachable subset enumeration via product:
        (5 Locality x 2 Access - 3 CN-8-eliminated Borrowed states)
        x (7 CN-1-canonical (Consumption, Cardinality))
        x (3 Uniqueness, with CN-6 selectively eliminating Unique on wide
           Locality x is_local-relevant rows)
        x (2 is_scalar)
      Bound from above: 7 canonical (Consumption, Cardinality) x 5 Locality
        x 2 Access x 3 Uniqueness x 2 is_scalar = 420 states (pre-CN
        filter); CN-6 + CN-8 + CN-1 jointly admit a reachable subset.
      Row 7 (true partition) canonical-row enumeration:
        is_local = true: 2 Locality (BlockLocal, FunctionLocal)
        Owned x Linear x Once x Unique x is_scalar=false (single canonical
          row per CN-1)
        = 2 x 1 x 1 x 1 x 1 x 1 = 2 states yield true.
      Rows 1-6 (false partition) canonical-row enumeration: balance of the
        canonical subset; the verifier enumerates exhaustively and confirms
        soundness equality on each.

    Negative-direction witness — Shared+Linear+Once counterexample:
      Consider s = (Owned, Linear, Once, Shared, BlockLocal, NonReusable, NONE),
      is_scalar = false. Per the predicate s.uniqueness = Shared violates
      fifth conjunct -> DP-7 = false. Per Appendix C Row 5 the same row
      yields false. Sound: caller's RcInc fires (DP-1 = true); the inc/dec
      pair is non-skippable here because DP-7's is_rc_skip_eligible requires
      Uniqueness = Unique, which this Shared state fails. Callee's RcDec
      elision (per RL-3 + DP-7) would leak the duplicate. Excluding via
      Uniqueness = Unique requirement is the gate that prevents this.

    ArgEscaping not-local witness (DP-8 composition):
      Consider s = (Owned, Linear, Once, Unique, ArgEscaping, ReusableCtor*,
      NONE), is_scalar = false. Per DP-8 is_local(s) = false (ArgEscaping
      in {ArgEscaping, HeapEscaping, Unknown}). Therefore DP-7 = false per
      Row 1. Sound: ArgEscaping arg participates in stack promotion in
      CALLER (per RL-15a) not callee RC elision; the inc/dec ABI obligation
      is preserved via the caller-stack header (immortal RC where required
      per RL-15a Owned branch).

    CN-6 wide-locality witness (HeapEscaping):
      Pre-canonical s = (Owned, Linear, Once, Unique, HeapEscaping,
        NonReusable, NONE) -> CN-6 demotes Uniqueness := MaybeShared ->
        post-canonical Uniqueness = MaybeShared -> Row 5 fail.
      Confirms CN-6 + DP-7 interact correctly: the Unique gate cannot be
      bypassed by wide-locality states (they canonicalize away from
      Uniqueness = Unique).

    Live-variable / borrow_sources / project_alias_sources / IC-3 contract
    typed pre-pass dependency: NOT REQUIRED for DP-7 (pure boolean predicate
    over canonical AimsState dimensions, evaluated on CALLEE parameter
    state; IC-3 / borrow_sources / project_alias_sources are upstream
    inputs to PARAMETER-CONTRACT derivation per IC-2 / IC-3, not to DP-7
    itself).

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix C row enumeration over 720 candidate
        product states with CN-1 + CN-6 + CN-8 canonical-filter pre-pass
        per section_05::verify_dp7_rc_skip_eligible; the verifier checks
        the soundness equality predicate-vs-row-partition on every
        enumerated state and emits Fail on any divergence)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_05 case_analysis engine discharges DP-7 via 720-state enumeration with CN-1 + CN-6 + CN-8 canonical filter; 7-row truth table; exactly 2 canonical rows (BlockLocal | FunctionLocal x Owned x Linear x Once x Unique x non-scalar) yield true per Annex E §AIMS DP-7 + Appendix C
